* enable-shutdown -- klt sim circuit body template (issue #366).
*
* Enable/disable behaviour and shutdown quiescent current for ldo_core with
* Xilimit (issue #11). Substantiates the ratified "Enable / shutdown" row of
* README.md's target specification: shutdown Iq, the settled disabled output
* state (pass device off, NO internal active discharge), and Vin->Vout
* leakage; plus the enable->active and active->disable transitions,
* including enable toggled at the full rated load, which is the condition
* under which a foldback limit could latch the regulator low.
*
* The shape `klt sim` accepts: no .control block, ONE analysis per corner
* (see sim/harness/klt_batch.py). The bench needs four analysis states
* (op / op / op / tran) of one circuit, so klt_run.py submits this body
* four times, one per analysis state, substituting the three tokens below:
*
*   state     @ENCTL@   @RLOAD@   @RFORCE@   analysis
*   enabled   1         36        1G         op
*   disabled  0         1G        1G         op
*   leakage   0         1G        1m         op     (Vin->Vout, output held at 0 V)
*   tran      PWL       36        1G         tran 1u 9m
*
* TRANSIENT WINDOW (widened by issue #38)
*
* Issue #11 wrote this bench against a design with no soft start, where the
* output reached regulation 28-64 us after the enable edge, and sized the
* enable window at 400 us accordingly. Issue #38 added design/ldo_softstart.sch,
* whose whole purpose is to turn that edge into a millisecond-scale controlled
* ramp, so the window here is 100 us -> 8 ms with a 1 ms disabled tail. The
* DC operating-point states (settled enabled, settled disabled, Vin->Vout
* leakage) are unaffected by that change -- they are `op` analyses -- so the
* shutdown-Iq and leakage numbers this bench owns stay directly comparable
* to the pre-#38 record. The per-clause startup measurements (ramp rate,
* inrush into C_out, overshoot, and the DR-0001 capacitor window) live in
* sim/soft-start/, the experiment that owns the ratified Startup row.
*
* THE LOOP-TIE AMMETER
*
* ldo_core's ERRAMP_OUT and PASS_GATE are deliberately separate loop-break
* ports that normal operation ties together (see design/README.md). This
* bench ties them through Vloop, a 0 V source, which is electrically the
* same plain wire sim/op-point-sanity uses but also meters the current
* crossing the tie.
*
* That meter is a diagnostic on the disabled state specifically. While
* disabled, Men holds PASS_GATE at VIN and the amplifier's output stage sits
* on the other side of the tie; any current crossing it is current the
* amplifier is still sinking from the pass-gate node, i.e. exactly the
* failure mode #9's un-gated amplifier had (its bias branch stayed alive and
* its M2N kept sinking). With #11's EN gating inside error_amp it should be
* leakage-level, and the bench prints it at every corner rather than
* asserting it.
*
* THE REFERENCE CURRENT IS METERED SEPARATELY AND ADDED IN
*
* VREF is an ideal 1.2 V source standing in for a bandgap that does not
* exist yet, so current drawn from it does NOT appear in i(vin) -- a real
* bandgap would source it from VIN. It is therefore added into the reported
* quiescent numbers rather than silently dropped. The bandgap's OWN
* quiescent current is not in any number here and never can be until that
* block exists.
*
* Issue #174 / DR-0021 moved that source from inside ldo_core (Vref1) to
* this body (Vref), so the meter reads i(vref) at the body level. Same
* source,
* same node, same sign convention, same number -- but it is metered AT THE
* PORT, which is what makes the iref_* measurements the load this block
* presents to whatever drives VREF (e.g. the Chipalooza Challenge #5
* bandgap-referenced bias slot) rather than an internal-node curiosity.
*
* EN follows VIN through an ideal behavioural source gated by ENCTL, so the
* request's supply axis can `alter vin` alone. The tran state's ENCTL is
* the exact edge shape (low to 100 us, high 101 us .. 8 ms, low after
* 8.001 ms), scaled by VIN. Solver options are the bench's own.

.include "dut.spice"
.options reltol=1e-3 vntol=1e-5 abstol=1e-11 chgtol=1e-14

Vin VIN 0 DC 3.3
Venctl ENCTL 0 @ENCTL@
Ben EN 0 V = 'v(vin) * v(enctl)'
Vref VREF 0 DC 1.2

Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 EOUT PG VREF ldo_core
Vloop PG EOUT DC 0

Resr VOUT n_esr 0.1
Cout n_esr 0 1u

Rload VOUT LN @RLOAD@
Vlmeas LN 0 DC 0

Vforce VF 0 DC 0
Rforce VOUT VF @RFORCE@

* Supply current in mA as a node voltage, so a top-level .meas can take its
* MAX (the bench's supply-current definition, -i(vin)*1e3 in mA).
Bivin IVIN 0 V = '-i(vin)*1e3'
